= Abstract

This paper describes a bounded-gain controller for a fictional thermal actuator benchmark. A proportional command is clipped to a fixed interval and evaluated in ten deterministic software runs. The synthetic mean settling time is 12.8 s and the synthetic mean absolute steady-state error is 0.42 C. These values demonstrate the paper_tools generation, table, figure, and export workflow; they do not establish hardware performance.

*Keywords:* thermal actuator, feedback control, synthetic benchmark, Typst
